From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 01/23] soc: mediatek: add MT6771 MCDI, SPM, SCP and LK framebuffer drivers

mtk-mcdi: keeps the SSPM's available-CPU mask in step with the online
CPUs and pauses MCDI (and cpuidle) across hotplug as MediaTek's kernel
does, and powers parked cores and empty clusters off through SiP calls.
Without it a core that enters PSCI power-down never wakes.

mt6771-spm: holds the AP's 26 MHz, bus and DRAM requests that the SPM
firmware holds on MediaTek's kernel (SPM_SRC_REQ 0x83), and optionally
(mt6771_spm.deep=1) starts the SPM firmware and suspends through it as
spm_go_to_sleep() does, refusing while a display, GPU or camera power
domain is still on; mt6771_spm.wake_mask sets the wake sources. From
cpuidle it enters the firmware's SoC idle states as MediaTek's
mtk_idle.c does: deep idle (CPU 0 alone, mt6771_spm.dpidle), SODI with
the display running (its CG mode, DRAM self-refresh alone, for a
video-mode panel; mt6771_spm.sodi) and SODI3 with 26 MHz down too
(mt6771_spm.sodi3), from the last core: mtk-mcdi checks that every other
core and cluster is off and pauses the SSPM's MCDI task meanwhile. At
probe it gates the infra clocks of those states' conditions that the
bootloader leaves running with no user.

mt6771-scp: starts the SCP and talks to its sensor hub; the
accelerometer, gyroscope, magnetometer, light and proximity sensors
become IIO devices with several buffers each. The SCP's own sleep is off
by default; mt6771_scp.sleep=1 leaves it on, with the MT6358's sensor hub
supply mode and the SCP's clock mux on its request, as MediaTek's
scp_dvfs.c does. The SCP runs on its own oscillators; its clock mux,
which also feeds the AP's bus gate to it, is parked on 26 MHz unless the
SCP asks for the PLL, so UNIVPLL can stop.

mtk-lk-fb: hands the bootloader's live framebuffer to simplefb, for a
console before the display driver binds.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig          |   44 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile         |    4 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6771-scp.c     | 1380 ++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6771-spm.c     | 1924 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-lk-fb.c      |  249 ++++
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mcdi.c       |  264 ++++
 include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk-mcdi.h |   17 +
 7 files changed, 3882 insertions(+)

